-- How `l4 render` and `l4 nlg` show `T WITHAL` on a record with no fields.
-- It checks to a named application with nothing written, so there is no field
-- list to show and no "where" to say: it reads as the record's own name.

DECLARE Marker HAS

DECLARE Holder HAS
  mark IS A Marker
  n    IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A Marker
`the marker` MEANS Marker WITHAL

GIVEN m IS A Marker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is marker` m MEANS TRUE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`check` MEANS `is marker` (Marker WITHAL)

-- An empty record as the value of a field in a record that has fields.
`a holder` MEANS Holder WITH mark IS (Marker WITHAL), n IS 1

#ASSERT `is marker` (Marker WITHAL)
